Let $k$ be a real number such that the system
\begin{align*} |25+20i-z|&=5\\ |z-4-k|&=|z-3i-k| \\ \end{align*}
has exactly one complex solution $z$. The sum of all possible values of $k$ can be written as $\frac{m}{n},$ where $m$ and $n$ are relatively prime positive integers. Find $m+n.$ Here $i=\sqrt{-1}.$

Find the largest positive integers $n$ that is no more than $2000$ for which we can fill in the entries of an $n \times n$ table with the following properties:

\begin{itemize}
  \item each entry can be one of $I, M, O$ and $P$;
  \item in each row and each column, the letters $I, M$ and $O$ occur the same number of times; and
  \item in any diagonal whose number of entries is a multiple of three, the letters $I, M$ and $O$ occur the same number of times.
  \item the letter P does not appear on any entry at all
  \item $n$ is divisible by $13$.
\end{itemize}

Show that there exists a sequence of positive integers $\{a_n\}_{n \ge 1}$ satisfying the following, and find the value of $a_{4096}$.
\[
    a_n = \begin{cases}
        1 & n = 1, 2, \\
        a_{a_{n-1}} + a_{n - a_{n-1}} & \text{otherwise.}
    \end{cases}
\]

Find all positive integers $n$ for which all positive divisors of $n$ can be put into the cells of a rectangular table under the following constraints:

\begin{itemize}
  \item each cell contains a distinct divisor;
  \item the sums of all rows are equal;
  \item the sums of all columns are equal; and
  \item the number of rows is a prime number.
\end{itemize}

